---
import BaseHead from "/src/components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "/src/components/sections/Header.astro";
import Footer from "/src/components/sections/Footer.astro";
import Projects from "/src/components/sections/Projects.astro";
import HeroSection from "/src/components/sections/HeroSection.astro";
import GlowLineSeparator from "/src/components/ui/separator/GlowLineSeparator.astro";
---


<html lang="en" data-theme="dark" class="dark">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title="Project 6: Cheese Wisely Coffee Table Book" description="Project 6" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <HeroSection title="Cheese Wisely Coffee Table Book" subtitle="A coffee table book with cheese related articles." />
      <GlowLineSeparator />
      <div class="project-content">
        <div class="hero-images">
      <img src="/project-6-cover.png" alt="Project 6 cover">
      <img src="/project-6-spread.png" alt="Project 6 spread">
        </div>
      <p>This design was created for my Advanced Typography class. We were tasked with creating a coffee table for a topic of our choice, using articles we found as it's contents.
        The topic I decided on this project was cheese, using articles surronding th health benefits of eating cheese. 
        One of the main focuses of this project was practicing the organization of the type and images, while maintaining the white space on each page spread.
        
        After completing the designs of the cover and spreads, the next step was print them out and spiral bind them into a physical book.
      </p>
      </div>
      <GlowLineSeparator />
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
.hero-images{
  max-width: max-content;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction:row;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
img {
  display: block;
  margin-left: auto;
  margin-right: auto;
  padding: 2rem 0 3rem 0;
  width: 65%; /* Optional: adjust as needed */
}
</style>
